1
00:00:00,467 --> 00:00:03,267
What if, right now, you could see exactly what was going to

2
00:00:03,267 --> 00:00:06,067
happen in the next 10 seconds? What would you do? Avoid an

3
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:09,900
embarrassing fall? Prevent an accident? Find out what your crush is about

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:13,167
to say? Or, use those 10 seconds to change something you might

5
00:00:13,167 --> 00:00:16,400
regret for the rest of your life? It sounds like a pretty

6
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:20,400
small superpower. But think about it. Ten seconds can sometimes change everything.

7
00:00:21,033 --> 00:00:24,333
The rule is simple. Whenever you focus and blink, you can see

8
00:00:24,333 --> 00:00:28,533
exactly 10 seconds into the future. Not a feeling. Not a prediction. You

9
00:00:28,533 --> 00:00:32,067
actually see what is about to happen. Then, you return to the

10
00:00:32,067 --> 00:00:35,933
present. And you have 10 seconds to decide: let that future happen,

11
00:00:36,033 --> 00:00:39,633
or try to change it. At first? You would obviously use this incredible

12
00:00:39,633 --> 00:00:43,800
power for the most important things in life. Like, not embarrassing yourself.

13
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:48,167
You see yourself trip. And somehow, the entire cup of coffee ends

14
00:00:48,167 --> 00:00:52,667
up all over your clothes. Even worse, someone nearby is already holding a

15
00:00:52,667 --> 00:00:56,533
phone. No. The internet does not need another meme today. You return

16
00:00:56,533 --> 00:01:00,133
to the present. Step slightly to the left. Avoid the crack. Perfect.

17
00:01:00,133 --> 00:01:05,267
You smile confidently. Having a superpower feels amazing. Then, you walk straight into

18
00:01:05,267 --> 00:01:09,800
a pole. BONK! Apparently, seeing the future still cannot save your dignity.

19
00:01:10,433 --> 00:01:13,967
During a meeting, you suddenly see your boss calling your name.

20
00:01:13,967 --> 00:01:18,100
You have exactly 10 seconds. Your brain instantly enters emergency mode.

21
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:21,700
You open the document. Scan the most important line. Ten seconds

22
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:24,867
later, "What do you think?" You sit up straight. Stay calm.

23
00:01:24,867 --> 00:01:29,700
And give a surprisingly intelligent answer. Everyone nods. Your boss looks

24
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:34,433
impressed. Congratulations. You just used a supernatural ability to look like

25
00:01:34,433 --> 00:01:38,633
someone, who was actually paying attention during the meeting. And honestly,

26
00:01:38,633 --> 00:01:40,533
that might be one of the best uses of this power.

27
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,233
Sometimes the power would help with much smaller things. You see

28
00:01:45,233 --> 00:01:48,100
your phone about to fall off the table. The screen hits

29
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:51,900
the floor. Shatters. You return to the present. Calmly reach out your

30
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:56,133
hand. The cat pushes the phone. And, you catch it. Perfect.

31
00:01:56,133 --> 00:01:59,400
Your superpower just saved you a few hundred dollars in repairs.

32
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:02,533
But from this point on, things start getting much more serious.

33
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:07,067
You are about to cross the street. The light is green. Everything

34
00:02:07,067 --> 00:02:11,233
looks completely normal. Then you blink. And see, a vehicle speeding out from

35
00:02:11,233 --> 00:02:14,300
a blind corner. If you keep moving, you are going to collide.

36
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:18,200
You return to the present. And stop. One second. Two seconds. Three. The

37
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:21,667
vehicle actually flies past you. Only a few feet away. And for

38
00:02:21,667 --> 00:02:25,667
the first time, you realize something. This power is not just useful for

39
00:02:25,667 --> 00:02:29,867
avoiding embarrassing moments. It could save your life. Maybe even someone else's.

40
00:02:30,767 --> 00:02:33,533
And of course, you would immediately think about sports. During a game, you

41
00:02:33,533 --> 00:02:36,167
see your opponent move to the right. Easy. You return to the present,

42
00:02:36,167 --> 00:02:38,833
and move right before he even makes his move. But there is a

43
00:02:38,833 --> 00:02:41,867
problem. He sees you move. So he changes direction. Left. Wait. That

44
00:02:41,867 --> 00:02:44,433
is not what you saw. And that is when you discover the biggest

45
00:02:44,433 --> 00:02:47,267
problem with your power. The future is not fixed. The moment you change

46
00:02:47,267 --> 00:02:55,533
what you do, the future changes too. Every decision creates a different outcome.

47
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:59,033
During a job interview, you see the next question. "What

48
00:02:59,033 --> 00:03:02,633
is your biggest weakness?" You have 10 seconds to prepare. This

49
00:03:02,633 --> 00:03:06,833
time, no awkward silence. No panic. You deliver the perfect answer.

50
00:03:06,833 --> 00:03:09,400
The interviewer smiles. But then you look 10 seconds ahead

51
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,867
again. And hear him ask: "Did you prepare that answer

52
00:03:11,867 --> 00:03:15,300
beforehand?" Okay. Maybe this power cannot save you from every interview.

53
00:03:16,267 --> 00:03:19,167
But some things are much harder. You are standing in front

54
00:03:19,167 --> 00:03:21,800
of someone you have liked for months. The words have been

55
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:25,367
stuck in your head forever. You blink. And see her reaction. "I'm

56
00:03:25,367 --> 00:03:28,533
sorry," Your heart drops. Now you have a choice. You could

57
00:03:28,533 --> 00:03:31,800
stay silent. Say nothing. Never get rejected. Never feel the pain.

58
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,933
But then you start thinking, if you avoid every future you do

59
00:03:34,933 --> 00:03:38,833
not like, are you really living? You take a breath. And say it

60
00:03:38,833 --> 00:03:43,467
anyway. "I like you." She pauses. Then, "I'm sorry. I'm just not ready

61
00:03:43,467 --> 00:03:49,900
for a relationship." Exactly what you saw. But this time, you smile.

62
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:54,900
Because at least now, you have an answer. Some futures do not

63
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:59,567
need to be changed. Sometimes, you just need enough courage to face them.

64
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:04,100
Then one day, those 10 seconds really change you. Your phone starts ringing.

65
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:07,067
It is your mom. You are busy. You think: "I'll call her

66
00:04:07,067 --> 00:04:10,600
back later." Your finger moves toward the decline button. But out of habit,

67
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:13,667
you look 10 seconds into the future. You see yourself rejecting the

68
00:04:13,667 --> 00:04:20,000
call. Walking forward. And behind you, an elderly man steps into the road.

69
00:04:20,133 --> 00:04:22,400
A truck is coming straight toward him. You return to the

70
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:25,467
present. You do not think. You run. Grab the man. Pull him

71
00:04:25,467 --> 00:04:28,033
backward. The truck flies past. Missing both of you by inches.

72
00:04:28,033 --> 00:04:30,967
You are breathing hard. The man does not even understand what just

73
00:04:30,967 --> 00:04:37,633
happened. You just saved someone's life. Then, your phone vibrates again.

74
00:04:37,767 --> 00:04:42,933
Your mom is still calling. You answer. "Mom?" There is a brief

75
00:04:42,933 --> 00:04:47,200
silence. Then she simply asks: "Did you eat yet?" That is it.

76
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:51,667
No emergency. No terrible news. No dramatic final words. Just an

77
00:04:51,667 --> 00:04:55,500
ordinary question. The kind of question you might ignore every day. You

78
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:59,133
laugh. "Yeah, Mom. I already ate." You talk for a few minutes.

79
00:04:59,267 --> 00:05:03,633
Nothing dramatic happens. But suddenly, you realize something. You spent

80
00:05:03,633 --> 00:05:06,233
the entire day staring 10 seconds into the future,

81
00:05:06,233 --> 00:05:09,367
and nearly ignored someone who was with you, right now.

82
00:05:10,167 --> 00:05:13,933
You thought the greatest part of your power, was knowing what would

83
00:05:13,933 --> 00:05:17,233
happen next. But it was not. Because even if you can see

84
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:21,767
10 seconds ahead, you still do not know what happens in 10 minutes.

85
00:05:21,767 --> 00:05:25,967
Tomorrow. Next year. Or when the last time you see someone, will

86
00:05:25,967 --> 00:05:30,067
actually be. And maybe, that is exactly what gives life its meaning.

87
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:33,833
Of course, seeing 10 seconds into the future is only a thought

88
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:37,533
experiment. It is not something we can actually do. In real life,

89
00:05:37,533 --> 00:05:41,100
there is no rewind button. No warning screen. No countdown telling

90
00:05:41,100 --> 00:05:44,267
us that an important moment is about to happen. But maybe, we

91
00:05:44,267 --> 00:05:47,633
do not need one. You can still look before crossing the street.

92
00:05:47,767 --> 00:05:50,200
You can still say what you really feel. You can call your parents.

93
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:53,467
Apologize to someone. Thank someone. Hold someone you love for a little longer.

94
00:05:53,467 --> 00:05:56,967
And sometimes, small decisions like those are enough to change the future. You

95
00:05:56,967 --> 00:05:59,367
do not need to see 10 seconds ahead to live a better life.

96
00:05:59,367 --> 00:06:05,500
You just need to stop wasting, the 10 seconds you have right now.

97
00:06:05,633 --> 00:06:08,000
"The future can wait. This moment can't." If you really could see

98
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:12,267
10 seconds into the future, what would you use it for?
